within ;
package ALOHA "ALOHA Stationary robot: complete mechanical assembly generated from public engineering sources"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Package;
  annotation (
    uses(Modelica(version = "4.1.0")),
    version = "1.0.0",
    Documentation(info="<html>
<h4>ALOHA Stationary virtual twin (kinematic / prescribed-motion formulation)</h4>
<p>Generated by the K&amp;KH ALOHA Engineering Studio generator v1.0.0 from pinned public sources:</p>
<ul><li>Interbotix/interbotix_ros_manipulators@b66d5b905725 (humble) interbotix_xsarm_descriptions</li><li>Interbotix/aloha@4fa6b2c4428f launch/aloha_bringup.launch.py</li>
<li>Interbotix/aloha@4fa6b2c4428f aloha/constants.py</li></ul>
<p>Assembly: 59 links (incl. world), 58 joints, 32 independently
driven joints, 4 mimic joints. Every URDF link maps to one <code>Components.RigidLink</code>, every
URDF joint to one joint component. Masses and inertias are the URDF values; URDF placeholder inertials are massless.</p>
<p>Run <code>ALOHA.Experiments.FollowerRightReach</code> (9 s). Meshes: Interbotix, BSD-3-Clause
(see Resources/Licenses).</p></html>"));
end ALOHA;
